{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1460583-auspiceless-urdaga","id":1460583,"title":"Auspiceless urdaga","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-20T14:58:28-07:00","id":1460583,"title":"Auspiceless urdaga","content":"So, I remember and example from The Pure 1st edition, where there was an ex pure now forsaken. <br /> No auspice, just tribe gifts and old gifts from the pure lists. (can't remember if Fire touched or Predator king)<br /> Would you allow such background? Is there any references about this kind of werewolves in 1st or 2nd edition book?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T02:45:20-07:00","id":1460626,"title":"","content":"Sure! The Lodge of Salvation from <i>Lodges: the Faithful</i> have deprogramming Anshega as their mission statement. They have a Rite that washes off the red marks of Pure Renown.<br /> <br /> I assume that such ex-Pure Forsaken will still be able to earn Renown from Lunes. As times goes by, their new allegiance will be visible on their skin, likely putting suspicious Forsaken at ease.<br /> <br /> Mind that in 2nd Edition Pure are said to have a deeper connection to their Firstborn, which takes root where their Auspice used to be. It's reasonable to assume that they can form an equally deep bond with their new patrons. Mechanically, it gives them an extra Tribe Gift and a Hunter's Aspect to replace the one from an Auspice.<br /> <br /> If you want to go really crazy, you can introduce Werewolves who remove their Auspices while remaining faithful to Luna. Their goal would be to dedicate themselves further to their Tribe patrons, just as the Pure do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 09-21-2021, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T05:41:53-07:00","id":1460638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1460583-auspiceless-urdaga?p=1460626#post1460626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure! The Lodge of Salvation from <i>Lodges: the Faithful</i> have deprogramming Anshega as their mission statement. They have a Rite that washes off the red marks of Pure Renown.<br /> <br /> I assume that such ex-Pure Forsaken will still be able to earn Renown from Lunes. As times goes by, their new allegiance will be visible on their skin, likely putting suspicious Forsaken at ease.<br /> <br /> Mind that in 2nd Edition Pure are said to have a deeper connection to their Firstborn, which takes root where their Auspice used to be. It's reasonable to assume that they can form an equally deep bond with their new patrons. Mechanically, it gives them an extra Tribe Gift and a Hunter's Aspect to replace the one from an Auspice.<br /> <br /> If you want to go really crazy, you can introduce Werewolves who remove their Auspices while remaining faithful to Luna. Their goal would be to dedicate themselves further to their Tribe patrons, just as the Pure do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, I'm a long time player and still I miss stuff from old and new books!<br /> I think that an auspiceless forsaken is a really interesting concept for a lot of reasons and also, can help people who want to play without feeling ''forced'' in a role. Yes the Pure are one with their totem, therefore they are also more united as tribes then the forsaken. This strong bond in 2nd edition was a great thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T11:34:45-07:00","id":1461061,"title":"","content":"Would I allow it? Well, it is the sort of character I have wanted to play for a long time, so probably! :P<br /> <br /> I like Teatime's suggestions a lot, though I personally wonder if it is even possible to remove the influence of a Pure Firstborn on your soul once it has wormed its way in? They do not exactly seem like the sort to release you simply because you no longer want to be a part of their club, but this is very much a &quot;whatever works for the story you want to tell&quot; situation.<br /> <br /> In particular, I wonder what Tribal Skills, Hunter's Aspects, and extra Tribal Gift the Forsaken Firstborn would bestow upon werewolves without an Auspice? It could be fun to brainstorm!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T10:10:27-07:00","id":1461233,"title":"","content":"SomethingFishy raises a good point about the hold Pure Firstborn have over their Werewolves. I remember asking on these Forums, whether one can change the Tribe they belong to, to the point of undergoing matching metaphysical changes. The consensus was that - yes it's possible, but it didn't consider the odds of Tribe patrons resisting. I think that Rabid Wolf is most likely to keep its claws deep in former Anshega, since it embodies faith and disease and is driven to spread wide. Silver Wolf, if anything like his followers, would likely drop the now tainted Uratha in disgust. I assume that Dire Wolf would be somewhere between its two siblings on this matter. Funnily enough, it's possible to follow Pure Tribal Bans even as a Forsaken. A story of a former Pure trying to honor their original Firstborn and Luna simultaneously sounds fascinating, and I'd like to see it somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T01:03:57-07:00","id":1461645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1460583-auspiceless-urdaga?p=1461233#post1461233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SomethingFishy raises a good point about the hold Pure Firstborn have over their Werewolves. I remember asking on these Forums, whether one can change the Tribe they belong to, to the point of undergoing matching metaphysical changes. The consensus was that - yes it's possible, but it didn't consider the odds of Tribe patrons resisting. I think that Rabid Wolf is most likely to keep its claws deep in former Anshega, since it embodies faith and disease and is driven to spread wide. Silver Wolf, if anything like his followers, would likely drop the now tainted Uratha in disgust. I assume that Dire Wolf would be somewhere between its two siblings on this matter. Funnily enough, it's possible to follow Pure Tribal Bans even as a Forsaken. A story of a former Pure trying to honor their original Firstborn and Luna simultaneously sounds fascinating, and I'd like to see it somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me one of the &quot;non-written&quot; differences from 1st to 2nd edition is the fact that relationships between pure and forsaken could be'... surprising.<br /> There are places where they kill each others on sights, places where they fight over dominance and territory and places where they also can be'... in good relationships. Writers also made the pure playable from dark eras. One of the best thing is the fact the pure are no more the boogiemen, the unstoppable hunter from the dark. They are just other werewolves with different philosophies and points , sure ,many of them are still zealots and ferocious beasts , but nothing the forsaken could not be. The pure hunt what they despise and what they think ruined the old Paradise, which is something interesting : the totem-Bond is something extremely strong which rise also from what their personality hided before the change, probably, mixed with primal urge, culture and who will find you, most likely. Tribe is everything for them, I suppose that leave Huzuruth , Hathis or Gurim would have consequences for the rest of your life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}